  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, but I couldn't run it. `node_modules/@aura3d/engine` is a broken link in this sandbox. The only typecheck error left is \"Cannot find module '@aura3d/engine'\". I could not check any engine call against its types, and I never saw a rendered frame. I used the engine API only as documented in the cheat sheet and the API signature docs.\n\n**Marble:** The pedestal has two steps, a shaft and a cap. It is one tessellated mesh with a colour per vertex. The colours come from layered value noise: domain-warped stripe veins, a vein mask, and cloud and grain terms. Veins continue across the steps. It uses a glossy `material.pbr` (roughness 0.16).\n\n**Trophy:** The foot, stem, knot and cup are lathe-revolved. Two handles are tubes swept along curves. A darker, rougher gold engraved band sits on the cup, with small rings at the stem and foot. The base is black polished stone with a thin gold plate. The gold is `material.pbr` with metallic 1, roughness 0.1 and colour `#ffc65a`.\n\n**Room and lighting:**\n- **Room:** A dark warm gallery with emissive windows, mullions and hanging lamps.\n- **Environment:** `environments.capture` builds the reflection environment from that room, taken once from above the trophy. Whether it renders correctly is the main thing to check first.\n- **Lights:** A warm shadowed spotlight sits above and in front. A cool fill, a subtle rim and a faint hemisphere light add to it. A small bloom is on.\n\n**Camera:** I did not find a documented way to move the camera at runtime. The camera is fixed instead, and a stage group (room, pedestal, trophy) plus the three light positions are rotated by the opposite angle each frame. That gives a ±15° orbit with a 24 s period. One difference from a real orbit is that the captured reflections stay still while the room moves.\n\n**State and flags:** `window.__TASK_STATE__` updates every frame with `materials: ['marble','gold','darkstone']` and the current `cameraAzimuthDeg`. `__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.rea",
